{"step_index":61,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T21:34:58Z","model":"gemini-4-argon-high","input_tokens":2871,"cache_read_tokens":52215,"output_tokens":1266,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: \"Plausible.Testable.check\" handles strings and booleans directly. Confirmed; it functions as expected. Additionally, Decidable instances for all properties are available, enabling both evaluation and bounded property-based testing.\n\n\nInitial suspicion was that direct evaluation over a test corpus would be complex, but decidable instances provide a simpler path. Creating decidable propositions for each property allows direct `#eval` checks with `Plausible.Testable.check` and bounded property-based testing using `native_decide` on the same properties. Validating these properties through decidable instances should cover all required test cases.\n\n\nTo ensure comprehensive coverage, create both randomized checks using the testing library and bounded examples for each property, including post-conditions, especially when implications are involved. Initial attempts at directly testing implications with randomized checks may lead to \"Gave up\" warnings due to the low probability of satisfying the implication's condition. Exploring alternative formulations or testing strategies is needed to overcome this. Acknowledging a need to define unescape.\n\n\nThe biconditional form `escape s₁ quote = escape s₂ quote ↔ s₁ = s₂` is significantly stronger than the conditional implication. This biconditional ensures that the test always evaluates to `True` due to the bidirectional nature of the equivalence, preventing \"Gave up\" errors during randomized checks. This is a critical insight for property testing. Proceeding to verify this biconditional property directly in the testing library.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cd /home/user/lean_project && lake env lean --stdin << 'EOF'\nimport Mathlib\n\ndef replaceChar (s : String) (target : Char) (replacement : String) : String :=\n  String.mk (s.data.flatMap (fun c => if c == target then replacement.data else [c]))\n\ndef escape (s : String) (quote : Bool := true) : String :=\n  let s := replaceChar s '&' \"&amp;\"\n  let s := replaceChar s '<' \"&lt;\"\n  let s := replaceChar s '>' \"&gt;\"\n  if quote then\n    let s := replaceChar s '\"' \"&quot;\"\n    replaceChar s '\\'' \"&#x27;\"\n  else\n    s\n\ndef injective_prop (s₁ s₂ : String) (quote : Bool := true) : Prop :=\n  (escape s₁ quote = escape s₂ quote) ↔ (s₁ = s₂)\n\ninstance (s₁ s₂ : String) (quote : Bool) : Decidable (injective_prop s₁ s₂ quote) :=\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (_ ↔ _))\n\n#eval Plausible.Testable.check (∀ (s₁ s₂ : String) (quote : Bool), injective_prop s₁ s₂ quote)\nEOF\n","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolSummary":"Test Plausible on biconditional injective_prop"}}]}
